{"id": "EUVD-2026-102268", "enisaUuid": "2a5e0f7b-2c3d-30ed-8091-0c38f71aba21", "description": "zziplib through 0.13.80 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in __zzip_parse_root_directory() in zzip/zip.c that allows attackers to read past the mapped central directory in mmap builds due to an ineffective bounds check. Attackers can supply a crafted ZIP whose entry name ends at the central directory end, triggering 28-byte ZIP64 extra field over-reads via zzip_dir_open() that crash the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:46:48", "baseScore": 5.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/zziplib-zip-central-directory-oob-read", "https://github.com/gdraheim/zziplib/blob/f58313c1f65f46bf73f3526d1afd4d6bb46cc4ae/zzip/zip.c#L530-L558", "https://github.com/gdraheim/zziplib", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zziplib-through-0.13.80-out-of-bounds-read-via-zzip-parse-root-directory-zip64-parsing"], "aliases": ["GHSA-25rw-cfg7-vc2v", "CVE-2026-111141"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ce797a93-9f2b-3a22-a5d0-aa01590bde11", "product": {"name": "zziplib", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.13.80"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ab3eb061-366e-3deb-8f4a-d2f19ed7e49b", "vendor": {"name": "gdraheim"}}], "isExploited": false}